From 0add091517d637c641e0f8a7c6550e7c5ea52bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ananth <ananth.chellappa@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:32:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] inpcom.c: carry the R model through the R->B rewrite

An R card whose value needs a behavioural source (it names v(), i(),
temper, hertz or time) is rewritten by inp_compat() into a B source.  The
B line is built from the equation, the instance tc1/tc2 and m only, so a
.model named on the card is dropped, together with its tc1/tc2/tnom, and
so are the instance dtemp/temp.  The converted resistor is flat with
temperature.  On ngspice-45.2, at 125 C, with 1 uA into each:

    .model rm r tc1=-2.47e-3 tc2=2.7e-6 tnom=25
    r1 a 0 rm r={73k*(1+1e-9*abs(v(a)))}    v(a) = 7.300000e-02
    r2 b 0 rm r=73k                          v(b) = 5.694000e-02

The converted resistor is 28% off.  sky130's xhigh_po is such a card.
pre-master-48 (a1148c969) gives the same two values.

The rewrite now carries the model, as text, because numparam has not run
yet and every value may be a {expression}:

- The .model lists that inp_add_levels() scoped are rebuilt for the
  rewrite (inp_rem_unused_models() has freed them, and a deck with .if
  never builds them), by the collection loop factored out of
  inp_rem_unused_models(), and freed again afterwards without commenting
  any model out.  A model may be defined after the instance.
- The model name is the token after one optional value (a number or a
  whole {...} group), accepted by is_a_modelname().  get_model_name()
  skips a {...} value too, so 'R n1 n2 {eq} model' keeps its model when
  unused models are removed.
- The lookup walks the card's scope outwards and accepts only an exact
  name; R has no binning.  The rewrite runs before .if is resolved, so a
  model written in both branches of an .if is found twice in one scope.
  Matches whose text after the name is the same, byte for byte, are one
  model.  Not found, or two matches in the winning scope that differ: a
  warning, and the line is exactly what it was before.  With the same
  .model rm in the .if and the .else branch of the deck above, at 125 C:
  v(a) = 7.300000e-02 and a "not resolved" warning if the second match
  is refused, 5.694000e-02 (= v(b)) with this patch.
- tc1|tc1r, tc2|tc2r and tnom come from the model; instance tc/tc1 and tc2
  override them per parameter.  A model tnom becomes an offset of the
  temperature the ASRC sees: dtemp={<dtemp|0>+27-(tnom)}, or
  temp={<temp>+27-(tnom)} when the instance gives temp, because the ASRC
  ignores dtemp when temp is given.  Without a model tnom, instance
  dtemp/temp are passed through; before, they were dropped even with no
  model.  Under '.option tnom' other than 27, a model without tnom keeps
  the ASRC's 27 C reference.
- A model with tce (not expressible) or one whose text uses temper:
  a warning, and the model is not applied.  An expression that uses
  temper while the model adds a TC the card does not show: both are
  applied, with a warning.
- Noise: the existing switch (set enable_noisy_r, or noisy=1) is
  unchanged.  When it is on and a model resolved, the 1 ohm resistor of
  the noise branch carries the model name and the instance's own
  tc1/tc2/dtemp/temp, so the real resistor device applies the TC, the
  tnom and the noise temperature.  With the switch off nothing is added.

A card without a model token is rewritten exactly as before.

Behaviour change: every R that is rewritten into a B source and names a
.model now has that model's temperature coefficients.  A PDK patch that
folded the TC into the expression by hand must be reverted.

Tests (tests/regression/temper, check.sh):
- temper-res-behav-1.cir: eight cases (top level, subckt with the model
  after the instance and a {expr} tc1, a .lib section, instance dtemp,
  instance temp, instance tc1 over the model, a model without tnom, value
  before the model) against references, at 0, 25 and 125 C, within 1e-9.
- temper-res-behav-noise.cir: the noise branch, off and on, against a
  plain model R, with dtemp and temp.
- temper-res-behav-noise-subckt.cir: the same in a subckt whose model
  shadows a global one.  A top-level R uses the global model, so that
  inp_rem_unused_models() keeps that card: a lookup in the wrong scope
  then finds the wrong model (maxerr 0.445) instead of none.
- temper-res-behav-dup.cir: the same .model in the .if and the .else
  branch, at the top level and in a subckt after the instance.  Refusing
  the second match leaves the converted R flat (maxerr 0.282, spread 0).
The decks keep vectors across 'reset' in the const plot (let const.x),
which needs 785be3194 (in ngspice-47 and later); their success line is
the tested branch, so a missing vector fails them.

Rechecked on pre-master-48 a1148c969: the four decks fail without the
patch (maxerr 0.314, 0.145, 0.156 and 0.282) and pass with it, the
wrong-scope figure above was measured there, and make check passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
